latestRelease.body:
## Highlights

### Factory Sandbox Provider Contract + New Providers (Docker/E2B/Platform)
Mastra Factory now has a first-class `FactorySandbox` contract for sandbox providers, enabling tunable settings schemas, repository templates, and prebuilt environment builds. New `*FactorySandbox` implementations ship for Docker (`@mastra/docker`), E2B (`@mastra/e2b`), and Mastra Platform (`@mastra/platform-workspace`) to plug in with a single provider instance.

### Factory Environment Builds + Multi-Repo Sessions
Factory can now build environment templates ahead of sessions (manual, scheduled cron, or push-triggered builds) when the sandbox supports `builds`, reducing first-session cold starts. Sessions also boot *every* repository in the environment (ordered, shared workspace root) and can push/open change requests across any environment repo via `source_control_*` tools with a `repository` slug.

### Durable Agent Safety: Run Fencing Across Storage Backends
Multiple storage adapters (Cloudflare DO/D1, Convex, DynamoDB, DSQL, MongoDB, MSSQL, MySQL, OracleDB, Spanner, Redis/Upstash/Valkey) now support “run fencing” so a durable execution that lost ownership (e.g., crash recovery) can’t overwrite the recovered run’s threads/messages/workflow state—significantly improving correctness in distributed deployments.

### Observational Memory Concurrency + New Conflict-Aware Storage Writes
A large set of fixes harden Observational Memory against overlapping buffering/activation/reflection across processes, adding “generation” protection (`supersededBy`) and new write-result APIs like `commitActiveObservations({ applied, reason })` and `appendBufferedObservations({ persisted, recordId })`. Observational memory also blocks less often (`blockAfter` band), preserves correct ordering, and improves reflection fidelity for long-running threads.

### Trace Linking & Cross-System Observability (Spans + MCP)
Spans now support `links` (including W3C `traceparent` helpers) and exporters propagate them (Datadog/Sentry/OTel bridge/exporter), enabling correlation across traces without joining them. `@mastra/mcp` additionally links client tool-call spans to server request spans bidirectionally, making it easy to navigate between agent traces and MCP server traces.

### Breaking Changes
- Factory projects now support provider-instance sandboxes (`MastraFactoryConfig.sandbox`) for settings/builds; existing callback form still works but lacks these capabilities.
- `@mastra/server` workflow HTTP routes no longer allow starting/resuming internal workflows (returns 404); durable agents must be invoked via agent routes (e.g., `POST /agents/:agentId/stream`).
- AgentController thread/session behavior changes include new suspension “address” claiming APIs and deprecations: `SessionRecord.modeId/modelId/state/pending`, `HarnessStorage.appendPendingItem/updatePendingItem/removePendingItem`, and `SessionSuspensions.resolveToolCallId()`.
- `@mastra/playground-ui`: `Dialog`/`AlertDialog` removed handle/render-style props; components are now controlled via `open`/`onOpenChange`.
- `@mastra/client-js` / `@mastra/react` compare-experiments APIs deprecate `experimentIdA/experimentIdB` in favor of `experimentIds` (+ optional `baselineId`).

## Changelog

### [@mastra/core@1.77.0](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/core@1.77.0/packages/core/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Minor Changes

- AgentController `steer` and `followUp` now accept file attachments, matching `sendMessage`. Attached files reach the model the same way whether the message is sent right away or queued behind an active run. (#26909)

  ```typescript
  await session.followUp({
    content: 'Then compare against this screenshot.',
    files: [{ data: screenshotBase64, mediaType: 'image/png', filename: 'expected.png' }],
  });
  ```

  The `/steer` and `/follow-up` routes accept the same `files` field and limits as `/messages`.

  _Also in: @mastra/client-js@1.54.0, @mastra/server@1.77.0_

- Added `FactorySandbox`, the contract a host implements to plug a sandbox provider into Mastra Factory. The bare callback that builds one `MastraSandbox` per session still works, but it gives a provider no way to expose tunable settings, a prebuilt repository template or template builds. A `FactorySandbox` owns all four, and lives in `@mastra/core/workspace` so provider packages implement it without depending on `@mastra/factory`. (#26467)

  **Required:** `provider` and `create`, which returns the session's `MastraSandbox`.

  **Optional:** `settings`, a schema of what a user can tune (zod, JSON Schema or Standard Schema; every field optional, absent means the provider default; no settings when omitted); `template` returns the environment's repository template for a context and settings; `builds` starts, reads and lists template builds ahead of any session.

  ```ts
  import { FactorySandbox } from '@mastra/core/workspace';
  import type { FactorySandboxContext } from '@mastra/core/workspace';
  import type { PublicSchema } from '@mastra/core/schema';

  interface Settings {
    region?: 'us' | 'eu';
  }

  class MyFactorySandbox extends FactorySandbox<Settings> {
    readonly provider = 'my-cloud';
    readonly settings: PublicSchema<Settings> = {
      type: 'object',
      properties: { region: { type: 'string', enum: ['us', 'eu'], default: 'us' } },
      additionalProperties: false,
    };

    create(ctx: FactorySandboxContext, settings: Settings) {
      return new MyCloudSandbox({
        id: ctx.sessionId,
        sandboxId: ctx.sandboxId,
        template: this.template(ctx, settings),
        workingDirectory: ctx.workingDirectory,
        region: settings.region ?? 'us',
      });
    }

    // Optional: the sandbox template image Factory can build ahead of time
    template(ctx: FactorySandboxContext, settings: Settings) {
      return myCloudTemplate(ctx, settings);
    }

    // Optional: build that template ahead of time and report on it
    readonly builds = {
      start: async (ctx: FactorySandboxContext, settings: Settings) => myCloud.startBuild(this.template(ctx, settings)),
      get: async (ctx: FactorySandboxContext, settings: Settings, buildId: string) => myCloud.buildStatus(buildId),
      list: async (ctx: FactorySandboxContext, settings: Settings) => myCloud.builds(this.template(ctx, settings).name),
    };
  }
  ```

- Added authenticated message authors to AgentController sessions. Pass `author` to `sendMessage`, `queueMessage`, or `steer`, and read it back with `getMessageAuthor`. (#26549)

  ```ts
  await session.sendMessage({ content: 'Hi', author: { id: 'user-123' } });
  const messages = await session.thread.listMessages({ threadId: session.thread.requireId() });
  const message = messages.findLast(message => message.role === 'signal')!;
  const author = getMessageAuthor(message);
  ```

- Added an optional `pricing` field to gateway provider configs. A custom gateway can now state what its models cost, in USD per 1 million tokens with the same keys as models.dev, so calls to private or reseller models get cost estimates. (#26875)

  ```ts
  async fetchProviders() {
    return {
      'my-provider': {
        name: 'My Provider',
        models: ['model-1'],
        apiKeyEnvVar: 'MY_API_KEY',
        gateway: 'private',
        url: 'https://api.myprovider.com/v1',
        pricing: { 'model-1': { input: 0.5, output: 1.5 } },
      },
    };
  }
  ```

- Added `links` to spans: references to spans in other traces. Pass `links` when starting a span to relate it to a span in another trace without joining that trace. Mastra storage saves the links with the span. (#26059)

  ```ts
  const span = getOrCreateSpan({
    type: SpanType.GENERIC,
    name: 'handle request',
    links: [{ traceId: callerTraceId, spanId: callerSpanId }],
    mastra,
  });
  ```

  Also added `parseTraceparent()` and `formatTraceparent()` to `@mastra/core/observability` for W3C `traceparent` values.

- Fixed observational memory losing context when a reflection, a buffered-observation write, and an observation activation overlap. The in-memory store now keeps buffered observations across a reflection, never lets activation drop a chunk written by someone else or move the observation cursor backward, and refuses observational memory lifecycle writes (buffered-observation appends, activation, active-observation commits, reflections) to a superseded generation. (#25906)

  Storage gained two methods that report the outcome of a write, plus optional inputs, so callers can detect these cases:

  - `commitActiveObservations` writes active observations and returns `{ applied, reason }`. It accepts `expectedActiveObservations` and never writes to a superseded generation.
  - `appendBufferedObservations` appends a buffered chunk to the current generation and returns `{ persisted, recordId }`.
  - `createReflectionGeneration` and `swapBufferedReflectionToActive` accept `newRecordId`; the reflection applied when the returned record has that id. `swapBufferedToActive` reports `retired`.
  - Observational memory records carry `supersededBy`, set when a newer generation replaces them.

  **Before:**

  ```ts
  const memory = await storage.getStore('memory');
  await memory.updateActiveObservations({
    id: record.id,
    observations,
    tokenCount,
    lastObservedAt: new Date(),
  });
  ```

  **After:**

  ```ts
  const memory = await storage.getStore('memory');
  const result = await memory.commitActiveObservations({
    id: record.id,
    observations,
    tokenCount,
    lastObservedAt: new Date(),
    expectedActiveObservations: record.activeObservations,
  });

  if (!result.applied) {
    // 'retired': a newer generation replaced this record. 'conflict': another writer changed it first.
    // Read the current record and observe again.
  }
  ```

  `updateActiveObservations` and `updateBufferedObservations` keep returning `Promise<void>`. In stores that implement the new methods, `updateActiveObservations` now throws when the observations were not written (the generation was superseded, or `expectedActiveObservations` no longer matches) instead of resolving as if they had been. An older `@mastra/memory` running against an upgraded store therefore reports a failed observation and observes the same messages again next turn, rather than marking them observed without saving their observations.

  Storage adapters that do not implement these keep their previous behavior. Upgrade `@mastra/core`, `@mastra/memory`, and your storage adapter together to get the full fix; every process writing to the same database needs the upgraded adapter.

- Added transferable AgentController thread ownership and a per-run owner snapshot in request context. New threads record their owner and creator, while ownership changes to the active thread become visible on the next run. (#26549)

  ```ts
  await session.thread.transferOwnership({ toOwnerId: 'owner-b' });
  ```

#### Patch Changes

- Fixed aborted agent streams reporting empty token usage. When a stream is aborted, `onFinish` now receives the usage of steps that completed before the abort: `totalUsage` is the sum across those steps and `usage` is the last completed step. Observability and cost tracking for cancelled runs now include that completed-step usage. Usage from the step that was still running when the abort happened is not reported. If no step completed before the abort, `usage` and `totalUsage` still have undefined token counts. (#26629)

- Update provider registry and model documentation with latest models and providers (`eaa9d12`)

- Added an optional `project_id2` to server feature and model-usage telemetry while preserving existing project identifiers and usage cursors. UUID-shaped `MASTRA_PROJECT_ID` values are sent unhashed with an `mp_` prefix for direct Platform lookup. Other values fall back to a hash of the normalized Git `origin` remote, discovered asynchronously without blocking startup. The field is omitted when neither source is available. (#22067)

  These events are project-linked, not anonymous. Git-derived identifiers can also be matched against known repository URLs. Set `MASTRA_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1` to disable telemetry and skip Git discovery.

- Fixed a tool running twice when the same suspended tool call is approved, declined, or resumed concurrently (for example a double click, a client retry, or two open tabs). `approveToolCall`, `declineToolCall`, `resumeStream`, and their generate variants now claim the suspended run before resuming it. Only one caller resumes; the others fail with `AGENT_RESUME_ALREADY_CLAIMED`. (#26688)

  ```ts
  const results = await Promise.allSettled([
    agent.approveToolCall({ runId, toolCallId }),
    agent.approveToolCall({ runId, toolCallId }),
  ]);
  // One fulfilled, one rejected with AGENT_RESUME_ALREADY_CLAIMED. The tool runs once.
  ```

  Durable agents report the losing resume the same way, as an error chunk in its stream with the `AGENT_RESUME_ALREADY_CLAIMED` id.

  What each resume error means:

  - `AGENT_RESUME_ALREADY_CLAIMED`: another approval or resume of this run is running or just finished. Stop retrying.
  - `AGENT_RESUME_RUN_NOT_SUSPENDED` (durable agents): the run exists but isn't waiting for approval, for example because it already finished or failed. `details.status` gives its state.
  - `AGENT_RESUME_NO_SNAPSHOT_FOUND`: there is no record of a suspended run. Check the `runId`. Agents delete a run's record when it finishes, so an approval sent after that also gets this error.

  Resuming a workflow run that isn't suspended now throws an error with the id `WORKFLOW_RUN_NOT_SUSPENDED`. The message is unchanged.

  Storage adapters that support atomic updates (for example PostgreSQL, LibSQL, MongoDB, and the in-memory store) protect against duplicates across processes. Other adapters protect against duplicates within a single process.

- Fixed durable, evented, and Inngest agents leaking one run's messages into another run's model prompt when two Mastra instances in the same process reuse a `runId`. (#26787)

  _Also in: @mastra/inngest@1.10.5_

- Fixed durable agents returning empty step data in callbacks and results. `onStepFinish`, `onFinish`, `onAbort`, `output.steps` and `output.response` now include each step's response messages and model id, the same as a regular agent. A `model` passed to a durable agent's `stream()` call is now the model that actually runs, instead of the agent's default model. (#26780) (#26933)

- Document that in-memory, LibSQL, and PostgreSQL workflow result updates no-op after run deletion while remaining adapters are aligned under COR-1448. (#26901)

- Fixed agent experiment results losing their error details. A failed agent run now stores `error.message` and `error.stack` instead of an empty object. Added exported `AgentExperimentOutput`, `ScorerExperimentOutput`, and `ExperimentResultOutput` types that describe what each experiment target stores in `output`. (#26726)

  _Also in: @mastra/client-js@1.54.0, @mastra/react@1.10.0, @mastra/server@1.77.0_

- Fixed output guardrails leaving blocked replies in memory. When an output processor aborts in `processOutputResult`, the agent (including durable agents) now deletes the reply messages that the run had already saved. The blocked text no longer stays in memory and is not sent back to the model on the next turn. This affected turns that paused for tool approval (approved or declined) and turns run with `savePerStep: true`. The user's message, earlier turns, and messages sent in as input are kept. Fixes #26215. (#26252)

- Added `targetType` to experiment results. The result `output` is now typed based on the target, so checking `targetType` gives you typed agent and scorer outputs: (#26726)

  ```ts
  const { results } = await client.listDatasetExperimentResults(datasetId, experimentId);

  for (const result of results) {
    if (result.targetType === 'agent') {
      console.log(result.output?.text, result.output?.error?.message);
    } else if (result.targetType === 'scorer') {
      console.log(result.output?.score);
    }
  }
  ```

  Workflow, processor, and caller-driven results (`targetType: null`) keep `output` as `unknown`.

  _Also in: @mastra/client-js@1.54.0, @mastra/react@1.10.0, @mastra/server@1.77.0_

- Workflow steps, conditions, and dynamic sleeps now create their `writer` stream only when your code reads `writer`. Steps that never use it no longer allocate a stream on every run, which reduces memory churn in agent loops. An agent turn, including a durable agent turn, now creates only the writers its tools use. Steps that call `writer.write()` or `writer.custom()` behave as before. (#26665)

- Fixed `mastra.datasets.compareExperiments()` silently comparing only the baseline and one other experiment. Every ID in `experimentIds` now gets a result entry on each item (`null` when that experiment did not run the item). Duplicate IDs are ignored, and passing a `baselineId` that isn't one of `experimentIds` now throws instead of being ignored. (#26725)

  ```ts
  const comparison = await mastra.datasets.compareExperiments({
    experimentIds: ['exp-baseline', 'exp-prompt-v2', 'exp-new-model'],
    baselineId: 'exp-baseline',
  });
  // comparison.items[0].results has entries for all three experiments
  ```

- Fixed evented agents and nested evented workflows failing with `Workflow with id ... not found` when an orchestration worker runs steps on the API server through `MASTRA_STEP_EXECUTION_URL`. The worker now sends the parent workflow with each step request, so the server can find steps that are only reachable through their parent workflow, such as the steps of an evented agent. Fixes #26676. (#26695)

  Also fixed nested evented workflows hanging when their parent workflow is registered under a key that differs from its `id`.

  _Also in: @mastra/server@1.77.0_

- Fixed delayed interruption of Evented agent responses while preserving partial output and graceful run cleanup. (#26926)

- Fixed core builds failing when regenerated model provider types grow large. (#26876)

- Fixed tools returned by an input processor's `processInputStep` (such as `ToolSearchProcessor`'s loaded tools) running with an empty `context.agent.agentId`. They now receive the agent's id, the same as tools assigned to the agent directly, in both regular and durable agents. (#26816)

- Fixed TypeScript types for Standard Schemas that transform their input, such as Effect's `Schema.toStandardSchemaV1(Schema.DateFromString)`. Tool `execute` functions now receive the transformed output type instead of a union of input and output types. Tool `requestContextSchema` now accepts these schemas, and tool request context is typed with the transformed output. (#26815)

  ```typescript
  const DateSchema = Schema.toStandardSchemaV1(Schema.Struct({ date: Schema.DateFromString }));

  const tool = createTool({
    id: 'schedule',
    description: 'Schedules an event',
    inputSchema: DateSchema,
    requestContextSchema: DateSchema,
    execute: async ({ date }, { requestContext }) => {
      date.toISOString(); // date is typed as Date
      requestContext.get('date').toISOString(); // request context value is typed as Date
    },
  });
  ```

  _Also in: @mastra/schema-compat@1.3.14_

- Fixed the `StorageMCPClientToolsConfig` and `StoredMCPClientToolsConfig` JSDoc. It previously said that omitting `tools` includes all MCP tools. For an agent-level MCP client reference, omitting `tools` selects no tools. Use `tools: {}` to include all tools. (#26738)

  _Also in: @mastra/client-js@1.54.0_

- `ExpectedStep` now supports `provider_tool_call` steps, so you can write typed trajectory expectations for provider-executed tools such as web search. The trajectory scorer compares their `toolArgs`, `toolResult`, and `success` fields. (#26778)

  ```ts
  const steps: ExpectedStep[] = [
    { name: 'web_search', stepType: 'provider_tool_call', toolArgs: { query: 'weather' } },
  ];
  ```

  _Also in: @mastra/evals@1.10.7_

- Fixed provider tool errors being sent back to the model as successful results. When a provider-run tool returns an error, Mastra now saves it as an error and sends it back as an error in later steps and recalled conversations. (#26652)

- Fixed live scorers missing tool calls when observational memory is enabled. Observational memory removes messages from the agent's context once it has observed them, and live scorers only saw the messages that were left. On runs that suspend and resume, scorer `output` could miss every tool call made before `suspend()`, or end up empty. Scorers now receive every response message the run produced, across all suspend/resume segments, under the original `runId`. The prompt sent to the model is unchanged. (#26687)

  _Also in: @mastra/inngest@1.10.5, @mastra/memory@1.37.1_

- Fixed reasoning from later steps being dropped when the reasoning text is empty. This affected providers that store reasoning identity outside the text, such as Anthropic, Bedrock and Gemini signatures or redacted thinking. Each distinct reasoning block now stays in the conversation when its provider metadata, provider options or reasoning details have an item ID, signature, redacted data, encrypted content or digest field. Identical reasoning blocks are not added again. (#26941)

- Fixed observational memory's temporal-gap reminder appearing after the user message it describes. A signal can set `metadata.precedesMessageId` to a message already in the conversation. That signal now sorts directly before the message in the prompt. Saved history keeps the same order. Models no longer read the reminder as the latest turn. (#26800)

- Updated the `observation.blockAfter` documentation for Observational Memory: between `messageTokens` and `blockAfter` only background buffering and activation run, and a blocking observation runs at or above `blockAfter` when no buffered chunk activates. (#22078)

- Fixed `structuredOutput` so it only uses the final answer of a run. (#26639)

  - Text an agent writes before calling a tool (like "Let me look that up.") no longer fails validation or ends the run early.
  - `stream.object` now resolves to the final answer, not an earlier JSON draft.
  - Durable agents now return the final answer instead of the first JSON they saw.

  (#25038)

- Fixed untilIdle streams dropping background tasks started by the run they replaced: a new stream({ untilIdle: true }) on the same thread aborts the earlier idle wrapper, and the new wrapper only tracked tasks whose events it saw itself — so an in-flight task's completion woke nobody and the agent never reported its result. The idle loop now adopts still-running and pending background tasks for its agent, thread, and resource when it starts, so their completions trigger a continuation turn as usual. Fixes #26841 (#26848)

- Preserve output processor retry metadata in durable step events (#26898)

- Improved AgentController sessions so each thread restores its saved mode, model, state, token usage, and pending tool prompts when selected. Switching away and `detachFromCurrent()` cancel actively running local executions only for the initiating session. Listeners detach without cancelling the run. Parked runs and pending prompts remain available when switching back. (#26058)

  Fixed first-thread creation to retain explicit startup mode, model, and thinking selections. Later new conversations use controller defaults. Asynchronous state writes and resumed tools keep their source thread's preferences without changing another active conversation. Addressed resumes recover the originating agent after restart and support repeated suspensions while another thread stays active. The executing run saves token usage to its own thread and retains unsaved measurements for retry on the next step. Subscribers display saved totals without counting replayed steps again or saving usage. Storage-free sessions can still receive inactive wake signals. Custom state and permissions remain host-scoped.

  Changed `session.thread.set()` and `session.thread.clear()` to throw during thread lifecycle transitions. Added address-based suspension APIs and event fields so callers can safely claim and resume a prompt after switching threads: `const claim = session.claimToolSuspension(toolCallId, runId)` returns an `address` that can be passed to `session.respondToToolSuspension({ address, resumeData })`. Exported `SuspensionAddress` and `getSuspensionAddressKey` for hosts that persist or key those addresses.

  Deprecated the `SessionRecord.modeId`, `modelId`, `state`, and `pending` fields, the `HarnessStorage.appendPendingItem()`, `updatePendingItem()`, and `removePendingItem()` helpers, and `SessionSuspensions.resolveToolCallId()`.

### [@mastra/ai-sdk@1.11.1](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/ai-sdk@1.11.1/client-sdks/ai-sdk/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Patch Changes

- Fixed v6 chat requests with several tool approvals stopping early. If another request is already resuming one approval, the remaining approvals now still run. (#26688)

### [@mastra/auth-better-auth@1.1.7](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/auth-better-auth@1.1.7/auth/better-auth/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Patch Changes

- security: bump better-auth to ^1.7.7 and @modelcontextprotocol/sdk to ^1.32.1 for Vanta/Aikido findings (AIKIDO-2026-373183, AIKIDO-2026-261025, AIKIDO-2026-365378/156139/344432). (#26773)

  _Also in: @mastra/mcp-registry-registry@1.1.5, @mastra/playground-ui@63.0.0_

### [@mastra/braintrust@1.3.21](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/braintrust@1.3.21/observability/braintrust/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Patch Changes

- Fixed the Braintrust exporter's `flush()` and `shutdown()` so they wait for Braintrust's background logger to send queued spans, scores, and abort updates instead of returning early. (#26759)

### [@mastra/clickhouse@1.25.0](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/clickhouse@1.25.0/stores/clickhouse/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Minor Changes

- Added `clickhouse_settings` to `ObservabilityStorageClickhouseVNext` and the other ClickHouse storage domains, so settings such as `filesystem_prefetches_limit` can be applied to every query without passing a pre-configured client. (#26327)

  ```typescript
  const observabilityStore = new ObservabilityStorageClickhouseVNext({
    url: process.env.CLICKHOUSE_URL!,
    username: process.env.CLICKHOUSE_USERNAME!,
    password: process.env.CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD!,
    clickhouse_settings: { filesystem_prefetches_limit: 8 },
  });
  ```

#### Patch Changes

- Fixed trace queries and trace aggregates dropping a trace when another tenant stored a trace with the same trace ID. Scoped trace queries and aggregates now read only that tenant's trace roots when picking each trace's current root. (#26327)

### [@mastra/client-js@1.54.0](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/client-js@1.54.0/client-sdks/client-js/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Minor Changes

- `client.compareExperiments()` now compares two to ten experiments at once against a baseline. Pass `experimentIds` and optionally `baselineId`: (#26725)

  ```ts
  await client.compareExperiments({ datasetId, experimentIds: ['exp-1', 'exp-2', 'exp-3'], baselineId: 'exp-1' });
  ```

  `experimentIdA` / `experimentIdB` still work for comparing two experiments, but are deprecated in favor of `experimentIds`.

#### Patch Changes

- Added the optional run id field to generated Agent Controller tool-suspension route types. (#26058)

### [@mastra/cloudflare@1.7.3](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/cloudflare@1.7.3/stores/cloudflare/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Patch Changes

- Added run fencing for durable agents. Durable Objects stores (`CloudflareDOStorage`) now reject writes from a durable agent execution that lost its run to crash recovery, so it can't overwrite the recovered run's messages, threads, or workflow state (#23734). (#26423)

  Claims are kept in two new tables, `mastra_workflow_run_owners` and `mastra_memory_run_fences`, which are created on init. If you set `disableInit: true`, create them before upgrading. Durable agent runs fail to start until the tables exist. `CloudflareKVStorage` doesn't support run fencing.

  `storage.prune()` doesn't cover these tables on Durable Objects yet, so their rows are kept.

  Requires `@mastra/core` 1.76.0 or a later 1.x release.

### [@mastra/cloudflare-d1@1.4.2](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/cloudflare-d1@1.4.2/stores/cloudflare-d1/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Patch Changes

- Added run fencing for durable agents. D1 stores now reject writes from a durable agent execution that lost its run to crash recovery, so it can't overwrite the recovered run's messages, threads, or workflow state (#23734). (#26423)

  Claims are kept in two new tables, `mastra_workflow_run_owners` and `mastra_memory_run_fences`, which are created on init. If you set `disableInit: true`, create them before upgrading. Durable agent runs fail to start until the tables exist.

  `storage.prune()` doesn't cover these tables on D1 yet, so their rows are kept.

  Requires `@mastra/core` 1.76.0 or a later 1.x release.

### [@mastra/code-sdk@1.13.0](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/code-sdk@1.13.0/mastracode/sdk/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Minor Changes

- The `theme` preference now accepts any theme name, not just `auto`, `dark`, or `light`, so callers can persist bundled and custom theme selections. (#26719)

- Added the `instructionRoots` session state field. A host that checks out several repositories under one working directory lists their directories, and the system prompt loads each one's `AGENTS.md` or `CLAUDE.md` in that order. Without it, instructions load from the working directory as before. (#26169)

  ```ts
  await controller.setState({
    projectPath: '/workspace',
    instructionRoots: ['api', 'web'], // loads /workspace/api/AGENTS.md, then /workspace/web/AGENTS.md
  });
  ```

  On an untrusted checkout with a `baseRef`, only the first root loads, from that ref.

#### Patch Changes

- Fixed cancellation of pending tool approvals to target the originating run and ignore prompts that have already been resolved. (#26058)

- The default memory from `createMastraCode()` now has a `settled()` method. Await it before closing storage so background memory work, such as buffered observations and their indexing, finishes first. (#22078)

  ```ts
  const { memory, storageMaintenance } = await createMastraCode();
  if (memory && 'settled' in memory) await memory.settled();
  await storageMaintenance?.closeStorage?.();
  ```

- New Mastra Code threads retain a stable local owner identity across sessions. (#26549)

### [@mastra/connect@1.0.2](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/connect@1.0.2/packages/connect/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Patch Changes

- Jira tool errors now include the human-readable message from `errorMessages[]` and field-level `errors` maps, and GitHub-style `{ message }` error bodies surface their message instead of a bare status code. (#26762)

- Fixed Linear tool calls failing on valid API responses: attachment tools now accept null creator emails, and cycle/project tools report GraphQL errors instead of crashing on validation. Fireflies transcript tools now handle `action_items` returned as either an array or a newline-joined string. (#26516)

- `@mastra/connect` now requires `@mastra/core` 1.76.0 or later, matching the `@mastra/mcp` version it depends on. (#26059)

### [@mastra/convex@1.7.3](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/convex@1.7.3/stores/convex/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Patch Changes

- Added run fencing for durable agents. Convex stores now reject writes from a durable agent execution that lost its run to crash recovery, so it can't overwrite the recovered run's messages, threads, or workflow state (#23734). (#26423)

  Claims are stored in the existing `mastra_documents` table, so no schema change is needed. Redeploy your Convex functions after upgrading. Until you do, durable agent runs fail with an error asking you to redeploy. Other writes keep working.

  `storage.prune()` doesn't cover these claims on Convex yet, so they are kept.

  Requires `@mastra/core` 1.76.0 or a later 1.x release.

- **Redeploy your Convex schema and functions when you upgrade.** This version calls new observational memory server operations and adds an optional `supersededBy` field; against functions deployed from an older version, observational memory writes fail until you redeploy. (#25906)

  Fixed observational memory losing buffered observations or activated context when reflections, observation activation, and background buffering overlap. Reflections and initialization now run as single server mutations, and every write checks that it targets the current generation. Older duplicate generations are marked superseded when a write targets them. Protection is complete once every process and the deployed functions run the new version.

### [@mastra/datadog@1.4.16](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/datadog@1.4.16/observability/datadog/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Patch Changes

- Datadog exporter and bridge `flush()` and `shutdown()` now wait a bounded time for dd-trace's background writer to send LLM Observability spans and evaluations, so a process that flushes and then calls `process.exit()` or gets frozen (serverless) no longer cuts the send off right away. The wait is best-effort: dd-trace gives no way to confirm the request completed. Tune it with the new `flushGraceMs` option (default 2000 ms, `0` disables): (#26761)

  ```ts
  new DatadogExporter({ mlApp: 'my-app', flushGraceMs: 3000 });
  ```

- Span links are now sent to Datadog as span links, from both `DatadogExporter` and `DatadogBridge`. (#26059)

### [@mastra/docker@0.11.0](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/docker@0.11.0/workspaces/docker/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Minor Changes

