### [@mastra/playground-ui@63.0.0](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/playground-ui@63.0.0/packages/playground-ui/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Minor Changes

- `Dialog` now opens as a bottom drawer on phone-sized screens (below 640px), so every existing dialog adapts to mobile without changes at the call site. People can swipe it down to close, the same as pressing Cancel. Pending dialogs still refuse to close. (#26765)

  **Removed props.** The same dialog can now render either way, so `DialogContent` no longer accepts `render` or a function `style`, and `Dialog` no longer accepts `handle`. Pass a plain style object, and control the dialog with `open` instead of a handle:

  ```tsx
  // Before
  const handle = DialogPrimitive.createHandle();
  <Dialog handle={handle}>
    <DialogContent style={state => ({ maxWidth: state.open ? 480 : 400 })}>…</DialogContent>
  </Dialog>;

  // After
  const [open, setOpen] = useState(false);
  <Dialog open={open} onOpenChange={setOpen}>
    <DialogContent style={{ maxWidth: 480 }}>…</DialogContent>
  </Dialog>;
  ```

- `AlertDialog` now opens as a bottom drawer on phone-sized screens (below 640px), the same as `Dialog`. Tapping outside still does not close it; swiping it down works like Cancel. Existing alert dialogs need no change. (#26768)

  **Removed props.** `AlertDialog.Content` no longer accepts `render`, a function `style` or `role` (it is always `alertdialog`), and `AlertDialog` no longer accepts `handle`. Pass a plain style object, and control the alert with `open` instead of a handle:

  ```tsx
  // Before
  const handle = AlertDialogPrimitive.createHandle();
  <AlertDialog handle={handle}>
    <AlertDialog.Content style={state => ({ maxWidth: state.open ? 480 : 400 })}>…</AlertDialog.Content>
  </AlertDialog>;

  // After
  const [open, setOpen] = useState(false);
  <AlertDialog open={open} onOpenChange={setOpen}>
    <AlertDialog.Content style={{ maxWidth: 480 }}>…</AlertDialog.Content>
  </AlertDialog>;
  ```

  `DialogContent` with `showCloseButton={false}` no longer reserves space for the missing close button next to the header.

- Added composable parts to `Avatar`: `Avatar.Image`, `Avatar.Fallback`, `Avatar.Badge`, `Avatar.Group`, and `Avatar.GroupCount`. Added `xs` and `control` sizes. Existing `<Avatar name="…" />` usage is unchanged. (#26619)

  ```tsx
  import { Avatar } from '@mastra/playground-ui/components/Avatar';

  <Avatar size="md">
    <Avatar.Image src={user.avatarUrl} alt={user.name} />
    <Avatar.Fallback>AM</Avatar.Fallback>
    <Avatar.Badge>
      <Avatar name={organization.name} src={organization.logo} />
    </Avatar.Badge>
  </Avatar>

  <Avatar.Group size="sm">
    <Avatar name="Jane Smith" src={jane} />
    <Avatar name="Sam Lee" src={sam} />
    <Avatar.GroupCount>+3</Avatar.GroupCount>
  </Avatar.Group>
  ```

  `Avatar.Badge` takes a `tone` (`neutral`, `success`, `warning`, `destructive`, `info`) for a status dot, or any child such as an icon or a small organization avatar. Avatars inside a group or badge take their size from it.

- Added `variant="inset"` to `Table` from `@mastra/playground-ui/components/Table`. It gives a native table the same raised look as `DataList`, with rows that grow with their content and cells that can hold any component. Existing default and small tables render exactly as before. (#26625)

  The inset variant comes with composable parts:

  - `Table.RowLink` and `Table.RowButton` make a whole row a link or a button, and other controls in the row keep their own clicks.
  - `Table.SortButton` turns a header into a sort control with a direction arrow.
  - `Table.Pagination` adds numbered pages below the table; the page and rows stay in your code.
  - `columnDividers` draws lines between columns.

  ```tsx
  import { Table } from '@mastra/playground-ui/components/Table';

  <Table variant="inset" aria-label="Credit history">
    <Table.Header>
      <Table.Row>
        <Table.Head>Type</Table.Head>
        <Table.Head align="end">Balance</Table.Head>
      </Table.Row>
    </Table.Header>
    <Table.Body>
      <Table.Row>
        <Table.Cell>
          <Table.RowLink href="/credits/1">Credit grant</Table.RowLink>
        </Table.Cell>
        <Table.Cell align="end">$6.95</Table.Cell>
      </Table.Row>
    </Table.Body>
  </Table>;
  ```

- Added `Pagination` at `@mastra/playground-ui/components/Pagination`: page navigation built from parts (`Pagination`, `PaginationContent`, `PaginationItem`, `PaginationLink`, `PaginationPrevious`, `PaginationNext`, `PaginationEllipsis`), plus `getPaginationRange` for choosing which page numbers to show. The current page slides between pages, and links can render as anchors or router links. (#26625)

  ```tsx
  import {
    Pagination,
    PaginationContent,
    PaginationItem,
    PaginationLink,
  } from '@mastra/playground-ui/components/Pagination';

  <Pagination>
    <PaginationContent>
      <PaginationItem>
        <PaginationLink isActive>1</PaginationLink>
      </PaginationItem>
      <PaginationItem>
        <PaginationLink onClick={() => setPage(1)}>2</PaginationLink>
      </PaginationItem>
    </PaginationContent>
  </Pagination>;
  ```

- Added a `size` prop to `ProductAvatar` and made it work inside `Avatar.Group`. In a group it takes the group's size and gets the same overlap ring as other avatars. Standalone `ProductAvatar` keeps its current size. (#26889)

  ```tsx
  <Avatar.Group size="md">
    <ProductAvatar product="studio" />
    <ProductAvatar product="observability" />
    <Avatar.GroupCount>+3</Avatar.GroupCount>
  </Avatar.Group>
  ```

- Added an `inline` variant to `DataPanel` that renders the panel in the normal page flow instead of a modal side drawer. Use it to embed detail views directly in a layout (no backdrop, focus trap, or dismissal). The parent controls mounting and size. (#26867)

  ```tsx
  <DataPanel variant="inline" title="Span details">
    <DataPanel.Header>
      <DataPanel.Heading>Span details</DataPanel.Heading>
    </DataPanel.Header>
    <DataPanel.Content>…</DataPanel.Content>
  </DataPanel>
  ```

#### Patch Changes

- Added a "Go to dataset" button to the toast shown after saving a trace, span or score as a dataset item. It opens the new item in its dataset. (#26866)

- Improved the main content layout on narrow screens. Where the sidebar collapses into the mobile header, the content is now flat and runs edge to edge under the header instead of sitting in an inset, rounded card. Wider screens with the sidebar beside the content are unchanged. (#26858)

- Fixed DataPanel headers on narrow screens. Header actions now wrap onto a second row instead of being pushed out of view, so every action, including the close button, stays reachable. (#26868)

- Fixed the `link` button variant so it is always a link. `Button variant="link"` now renders an `<a>` with an href even when no link element is passed, instead of a button that only looked like one. A disabled link keeps its href and is marked `aria-disabled`. (#26817)

- Fixed `PageHeader` shifting between pages. The title row is now 32px tall with the title in the same position whether or not the header has an icon or `PageHeader.Action`, so moving between pages no longer moves the title. `PageLayout` also reserves the scrollbar gutter in its scroll area, so a narrow, centered column no longer shifts sideways when a page starts to scroll. (#26915)

- Fixed the filter bar adding a second chip for a field that already has one. On pages that keep one filter per field (Logs, Metrics, Traces), picking another value for an already filtered field now updates its chip instead of adding a chip that is silently ignored: values combine into "is any of" when the field supports it, otherwise the new value replaces the old one. (#26513)

  The Traces page also keeps "is any of" filters on Status and Primitive type in the URL. Before, they were dropped and the list stayed unfiltered.

  Operators declare their multi-value form with the new `widensTo` option:

  ```ts
  const operators = [
    { id: 'is', label: 'is', widensTo: 'in' },
    { id: 'in', label: 'is any of', arity: 'many' },
  ];
  ```

- The inline `DataPanel` now uses the same rounded corners as the app frame, so it lines up with the main card when it sits next to it. The drawer keeps its current corners. (#26887)

- Trace Intelligence now labels its list by Agent instead of Entity. Agents whose traces are still being analyzed show an "Analyzing" status and can no longer be clicked, since they have no signals to open yet. Hovering or focusing the status shows how many traces have been collected. (#26812)

