- Forward authenticated users as AgentController message authors. (#26549)

- Added an optional run id to tool-suspension responses so callers can target the exact suspended run when tool-call ids are reused. (#26058)

- Workflow HTTP routes and `POST /schedules` no longer resolve internal workflows (such as a durable agent's `durable-agentic-loop` or the notification dispatcher). These now return 404, so agent runs can't be started or resumed through `/workflows/*` in a way that skips the agent routes' scope, ownership and approval checks. (#26940)

  If you called a durable agent's loop through the workflow routes, use the agent routes instead:

  ```diff
  - POST /workflows/durable-agentic-loop/start-async
  + POST /agents/:agentId/stream

  - POST /workflows/durable-agentic-loop/resume-async
  + POST /agents/:agentId/resume-stream
  ```

- Fixed losing concurrent tool approvals and agent resumes returning HTTP 500. The approve, decline, and resume routes now return 409 Conflict when another request is already resuming the same run, or when the run isn't waiting to be resumed. (#26688)

### [@mastra/spanner@1.9.4](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/spanner@1.9.4/stores/spanner/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Patch Changes

- Added run fencing for durable agents. Spanner stores now reject writes from a durable agent execution that lost its run to crash recovery, so it can't overwrite the recovered run's messages, threads, or workflow state (#23734). (#26421)

  Claims are kept in two new tables, `mastra_workflow_run_owners` and `mastra_memory_run_fences`, which are created on init. If you set `disableInit: true`, create them before upgrading. Durable agent runs fail to start until the tables exist.

  `storage.prune()` doesn't cover these tables on Spanner yet, so their rows are kept.

  Requires `@mastra/core` 1.76.0 or a later 1.x release.

### [@mastra/upstash@1.5.3](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/upstash@1.5.3/stores/upstash/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Patch Changes

- Added run fencing for durable agents. Upstash stores now reject writes from a durable agent execution that lost its run to crash recovery, so it can't overwrite the recovered run's messages, threads, or workflow state (#23734). (#26422)

  Claims are stored as keys in the same database, so no setup is needed.

  Claims and memory fences expire on their own: a claim 7 days after its last claim, renewal or release, and a fence 7 days after it is retired. Running executions renew their claim every few seconds, and fences of unfinished runs never expire. `storage.prune()` doesn't manage these keys, and the 7 days aren't configurable.

  Requires `@mastra/core` 1.76.0 or a later 1.x release.

